WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.913
Ablations probe the privacy-accuracy trade-off.

00:00:03.993 --> 00:00:07.905
Sweeping noise variance,

00:00:07.985 --> 00:00:11.898
DP-CutMixSL has the best accuracy at nearly every
level and always beats DP-MixSL.

00:00:11.978 --> 00:00:15.891
Its RDP epsilon is tighter than DP-SL but looser
than DP-MixSL,

00:00:15.971 --> 00:00:19.884
exactly the trade-off theory predicts,

00:00:19.964 --> 00:00:23.876
since Mixup melts information across the whole
representation.

00:00:23.956 --> 00:00:27.869
Larger mixing groups lower both accuracy and
epsilon, a hiding-in-the-crowd effect.

00:00:27.949 --> 00:00:31.862
A reconstruction attack shows robustness rising
from raw data to Mixup, patch CutMix,

00:00:31.942 --> 00:00:35.855
then Cutout.

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:39.847
Finally, accuracy grows as clients scale from two to ten,

00:00:39.927 --> 00:00:43.840
and SplitFed-style averaging helps further.
